            "diff_url": "https://github.com/date-fns/date-fns/pull/4339.diff",
            "patch_url": "https://github.com/date-fns/date-fns/pull/4339.patch",
            "merged_at": null
          },
          "body": "Expose `timeZone: \"UTC\"` on `UTCDateMini`, inherited by `UTCDate`, with a read-only literal type. The Temporal adapter can then preserve UTC when cloning either class or using the `utc` context, rather than falling back to the host zone and choosing the wrong ISO week-year.\n\nFixes #4338.\n\nValidation on Node 26.10.0 with `TZ=America/Los_Angeles`: three result regressions and two metadata cases fail before the fix. Afterward, all 822 Temporal tests pass with `--testTimeout15000`, and all 36 UTC tests pass (four existing todos). Direct checks also pass in UTC, Berlin and Kathmandu. Package and consumer type checks, type-aware lint and formatting pass.\n",
